@kow3ns We shouldn't promote the annotation to a field and then change the semantics afterward. 

Why not a PublishNotReadyAddresses field (to match the name of the Endpoints field), which DNS could use to make the decision? We could leave the existing alpha annotation as is until the consumers we care about transition to the new approach. 

The NotReadyAddresses field was added 2 years ago, in #13778.

@smarterclayton I have a use case where a container has a control port and a service port. The service port isn't "ready" until something attaches to the control port, loads some data, and executes a "make ready" API call.

Right now, this is handled by using this annotation for the control port service and not using it for the service port service. This is fine for me because my control port client just has to handle the possible non-readiness of the control port. But in theory this sort of use case would imply per-service readiness checks rather than per-container readiness checks.

The "juice may not be worth the squeeze" for that one, though.

